reddit is the ultimate source of  information you choose what kind of  content you care about and the world  votes on what pieces of information are  noteworthy because reddit is so  democratic bad content is filtered out  and you see only the best a person's  authority and integrity is decided by  their karma a measure of the success of  their posts someone with many lousy  posts will receive lots of down votes  giving them a negative karma and telling  users to be wary of their posts in the  future there is a bit of a problem  though people vote based on their  agreement with content instead of its  quality so because you want your post  seen and don't want your comic to drop  your pressured into posting not what you  think but what the community wants once  an idea has just barely a majority of  support it can dominate reddit thinking  by becoming the most popular opinion an  idea becomes what the community wants  and the cycle continues post will be  catered to that idea out of social  pressure and all dissenting opinions  will be silenced if opinion a has 40  percent support opinion be 31% and see  twenty nine opinion a will become  popular opinion and swallow almost all  discussion on the topic opinion a may  receive 90% of posts and up votes  because of its lead however small but  bystanders will reasonably assume it  means 90% of the community supports  opinion a you can expect a plethora of  different political opinions from the  three million people and 11,000 separate  communities within Reddit but this  spread isn't apparent out of the popular  political posts in 2015 almost all  support a single candidate given  reddit's leanings it does make sense  that the most liberal candidate has a  disproportionate amount of support but  the fact that there is almost no other  opinion posted suggests not that it  doesn't exist but that people are afraid  to post against the majority a study on  reddit social influence found that the  first votes on a post largely 